// Bans hand-written `orgId` / `projectId` filters inside a Prisma `where` clause
// on the request-scoped Prisma client.
//
// Tenant isolation is owned by the scoped Prisma client (`createScopedClient`,
// packages/db/src/scoped-client.ts), exposed on the request context. It
// auto-injects `orgId` for every model in ORG_TENANT_MODELS and `projectId` for
// every model in PROJECT_TENANT_MODELS. Re-filtering by hand is at best
// redundant and at worst hides a model that was never registered for
// auto-scoping — the default-open cross-tenant leak the DMMF completeness test
// (packages/db/src/scoped-models.test.ts) exists to prevent.
//
// Scope: only flags calls on the always-scoped request client
// (`ctx.db` / `ctx.prisma` / `ctx.scopedPrisma`) — never the unscoped singleton
// `prisma` used by seed, workers, auth and admin, which MUST filter by hand.
// Only read/write `where` clauses are flagged (not `create` / `upsert` data,
// which MUST set the tenant column). A where assembled into a separate variable
// is not caught — the DMMF completeness test is the authoritative guard; this
// rule is the fast in-editor feedback.
//
// If the model is genuinely not auto-scoped (intentionally cross-tenant, or in
// INTENTIONALLY_UNSCOPED), opt out with `// biome-ignore lint/plugin: <reason>`
// on the line above the filter. (Biome 2.5 groups all plugin diagnostics under
// the `lint/plugin` suppression category — there is no per-rule selector.)
language js

`$client.$model.$method($args)` where {
  $client <: or {
    `ctx.db`,
    `ctx.prisma`,
    `ctx.scopedPrisma`
  },
  $method <: or {
    `findFirst`,
    `findMany`,
    `findUnique`,
    `findFirstOrThrow`,
    `findUniqueOrThrow`,
    `count`,
    `aggregate`,
    `groupBy`,
    `update`,
    `updateMany`,
    `delete`,
    `deleteMany`,
    `upsert`
  },
  $args <: contains `where: $where`,
  $where <: contains or {
    `orgId: $value`,
    `projectId: $value`
  } as $hit,
  register_diagnostic(span=$hit, message="Do not hand-filter `orgId`/`projectId` in a Prisma where clause — rely on the scoped Prisma client (ctx.db / ScopedPrismaClient), which auto-scopes every model in ORG_TENANT_MODELS / PROJECT_TENANT_MODELS. If this uses the unscoped `prisma` singleton (seed/auth/system) or is intentionally cross-tenant, suppress with a biome-ignore explaining why.", severity="error")
}
